// read model has consumed the store, and means the same over any transport; a
// Since is where in the repository that consumption was read from, and is git's.
//
// The erasures are carried because they are the one answer a read cannot give
// from the new entries alone. A batch restates every erasure in force, and the
// set is drawn from the newest generation and every entry in the tail — most of
// which a reader that kept nothing no longer holds. Between two reads the set
// only grows by what the new entries carry: it shrinks by discharge, and
// discharge happens at compaction and prune, which publish a generation or
// rotate a log, which is a whole read.
